BSP-Yocto-TISDK-AM62x-ALPHA1                    2022-10-04
==========================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v5.10.120 (based on TI tag 08.04.01.002)
- U-Boot v2021.01 (based on TI tag 08.03.00.005)
- Yocto 3.1.12 (dunfell, based on TI CoreSDK 08.03.00.005)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working or stable. This release will NOT
be supported after the first full BSP release.


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- tisdk-default-image:
  * phyboard-lyra-am62xx-1


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 18.04 64-bit


Features:
---------

- Added support for new machine:
  * phyboard-lyra-am62xx-1
- Booting from eMMC and MMC/SD supported
- Support for the following features:
  * RAM
  * eMMC Flash
  * Micro SD Card
  * OSPI Flash
  * GPU
  * USB 2.0
  * USB C
  * MIPI-CSI (+VM-016-M)
  * OLDI/LVDS
  * Ethernet
  * HDMI
  * McASP
  * ePWM
  * WiFi
  * I2C
  * UART
  * User GPIOs
  * RTC

Known Issues:
-------------

- OSPI Boot is failing
- Having identical wic image flashed on eMMC and inserted SD card
  leads to a boot failure due to identical partition UUIDs
- Bluetooth and MCAN is non functional
